  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Departments within the people's governments involved in statistical and archive administration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e892165d5d39fe39325131368a7c8e29</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ILLEGAL ACT&quot;">
  <data key="d2">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
  <data key="d1">"Illegal acts are recorded in credit archives."</data>
  <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
</node>
<edge source="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d3">16.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The law applies within the territory of the People's Republic of China."</data>
  <data key="d5">"law jurisdiction, geographical scope"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;STATE CYBERSPACE ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">29.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The State cyberspace administration is a governmental organization within the People's Republic of China, responsible for regulating personal information processing within its territory."&lt;SEP&gt;"The State cyberspace administration operates within and enforces regulations across the People's Republic of China regarding personal information processing."</data>
  <data key="d5">"governance, jurisdiction"&lt;SEP&gt;"jurisdiction, governance"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;STATE ORGAN&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"State organs operate within the People's Republic of China and are subject to its laws regarding personal information processing."</data>
  <data key="d5">"governance, geographic location"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;FOREIGN JUDICIAL OR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES&quot;">
  <data key="d3">14.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The People's Republic of China handles requests from foreign judicial or law enforcement agencies for personal information stored within its territory according to its laws and international agreements.  This relationship is subject to approval from competent authorities within the PRC."</data>
  <data key="d5">"international cooperation, data sharing"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;OVERSEAS ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL&quot;">
  <data key="d3">16.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The People's Republic of China may take measures against overseas organizations or individuals whose actions damage the rights of Chinese citizens or endanger national security."</data>
  <data key="d5">"national security, legal protection"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;13TH NATIONAL PEOPLE'S CONGRESS&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d3">14.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The 13th National People's Congress is the legislative body to which the Standing Committee belongs, and thus indirectly involved in the law's adoption."</data>
  <data key="d5">"legislative process, hierarchical relationship"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STANDING COMMITTEE OF THE 13TH NATIONAL PEOPLE'S CONGRESS&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d3">18.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The Standing Committee adopted the Personal Information Protection Law at its 30th meeting."</data>
  <data key="d5">"law adoption, legislative process"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;XI JINPING&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d3">20.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Xi Jinping, as President, promulgated the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"law promulgation, executive action"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;AUGUST 20, 2021&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The law was adopted and promulgated on this date."</data>
  <data key="d5">"law enactment, timeline"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION LAW OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;" target="&quot;NOVEMBER 1, 2021&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The law came into force on this date."</data>
  <data key="d5">"law enforcement, timeline"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;NATURAL PERSON&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d3">12.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A natural person can also be a personal information processor, but only in the context of their personal or family affairs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Processors are responsible for the security and ethical handling of a natural person's personal information."</data>
  <data key="d5">"data protection, responsibility"&lt;SEP&gt;"legal exception, personal scope"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e892165d5d39fe39325131368a7c8e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDIVIDUAL&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d3">35.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Personal information processors collect, process, and store the personal information of individuals, subject to the regulations and rights of the individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The personal information processor processes the personal information of the individual, requiring the individual's consent and notification of data usage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The personal information processor processes the personal information of the individual, subject to the consent of the individual and various legal requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The processor handles the individual's data; the individual has rights regarding that data."</data>
  <data key="d5">"Data handling, individual rights"&lt;SEP&gt;"data processing, consent"&lt;SEP&gt;"data processing, consent, notification"&lt;SEP&gt;"data processing, individual rights"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDIVIDUAL&quot;" target="&quot;WITHDRAWAL OF CONSENT&quot;">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The individual can revoke previously granted consent."</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consent revocation, data control"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;INDIVIDUAL&quot;" target="&quot;NEAR RELATIVES&quot;">
  <data key="d3">6.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Upon the death of an individual, their near relatives may exercise certain rights related to the deceased's personal information."</data>
  <data key="d5">"inheritance, data rights"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d3">18.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Processors must obtain consent from the minor's parent or guardian before processing a minor's personal information."&lt;SEP&gt;"The personal information processor must obtain consent from the parent or guardian before processing a minor's personal information."</data>
  <data key="d5">"data protection, consent"&lt;SEP&gt;"data protection, consent, minors"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR&quot;" target="&quot;PARENT OR OTHER GUARDIAN&quot;">
  <data key="d3">10.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Parents or guardians have legal responsibility for consenting to the processing of a minor's personal information."</data>
  <data key="d5">"legal guardianship, consent"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b2a8064a6294712d680163c4e5f2b061</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;MINOR (BELOW 14)&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The personal information processor must obtain consent from the minor's parent or guardian before processing the minor's personal information."</data>
  <data key="d5">"parental consent, data protection"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONSENT&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The processor requires consent before processing data in most cases."</data>
  <data key="d5">"Consent, data processing"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 17&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The processor must follow the notification requirements in Article 17."</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal obligation, notification"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;ARTICLE 20&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Article 20 details the responsibilities of multiple processors."</data>
  <data key="d5">"Joint responsibility, data processing"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;OVERSEAS RECIPIENT&quot;">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A personal information processor may transfer personal information to an overseas recipient only under specific conditions and with appropriate safeguards."</data>
  <data key="d5">"data transfer, cross-border"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;STATE CYBERSPACE ADMINISTRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">40.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Personal information processors are subject to the supervision and administration of the state cyberspace administration."&lt;SEP&gt;"The State cyberspace administration regulates and oversees the activities of personal information processors, including cross-border data transfers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The State cyberspace administration sets regulations and requirements for personal information processors, including security assessments and data storage locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state cyberspace administration designates an organization to file lawsuits against violating personal information processors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The state cyberspace administration oversees personal information processors and their compliance with the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"legal authority, oversight"&lt;SEP&gt;"regulation, compliance"&lt;SEP&gt;"regulation, oversight"&lt;SEP&gt;"regulatory oversight, compliance"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e892165d5d39fe39325131368a7c8e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;PERSON IN CHARGE OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A personal information processor designates a person in charge to supervise personal information processing and protection measures."</data>
  <data key="d5">"responsibility, supervision"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A personal information processor outside China designates a representative within China to handle personal information protection matters."</data>
  <data key="d5">"representation, compliance"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;LAWS AND ADMINISTRATIVE REGULATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">10.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Personal information processors must comply with all applicable laws and administrative regulations regarding personal information processing."</data>
  <data key="d5">"compliance, legal framework"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;PEOPLE'S COURT&quot;">
  <data key="d3">17.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A personal information processor who violates the law may face legal action in the people's court."&lt;SEP&gt;"The people's court determines compensation amounts in cases where a personal information processor violates the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"legal accountability, judicial process"&lt;SEP&gt;"legal recourse, compensation"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e892165d5d39fe39325131368a7c8e29</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;PEOPLE'S PROCURATORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d3">18.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A personal information processor who violates the law may face legal action from the people's procuratorate."&lt;SEP&gt;"The people's procuratorate can file lawsuits against personal information processors for violating the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"legal accountability, judicial process"&lt;SEP&gt;"legal action, violation of law"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e892165d5d39fe39325131368a7c8e29</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;" target="&quot;CONSUMER ORGANIZATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">17.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"A personal information processor who violates the law may face legal action from consumer organizations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumer organizations can file lawsuits against personal information processors for violating the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"legal accountability, consumer protection"&lt;SEP&gt;"legal action, violation of law"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e892165d5d39fe39325131368a7c8e29</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MINOR (BELOW 14)&quot;" target="&quot;PARENT OR GUARDIAN&quot;">
  <data key="d3">10.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The parent or guardian provides consent for the processing of the minor's personal information."</data>
  <data key="d5">"parental consent, legal guardianship"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ARTICLE 15&quot;" target="&quot;WITHDRAWAL OF CONSENT&quot;">
  <data key="d3">10.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Article 15 legally defines the right to withdrawal of consent."</data>
  <data key="d5">"Legal basis, consent"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-8ff4e3011eeb0855c4ad54f1eb00bbe3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE CYBERSPACE ADMINISTRATION&quot;" target="&quot;STATE ORGAN&quot;">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The State cyberspace administration sets standards and regulations that govern how State organs process personal information within the People's Republic of China."</data>
  <data key="d5">"regulation, oversight"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE CYBERSPACE ADMINISTRATION&quot;" target="&quot;CRITICAL INFORMATION INFRASTRUCTURE OPERATORS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Critical information infrastructure operators are subject to the regulations and security assessments of the State cyberspace administration regarding cross-border data transfers."</data>
  <data key="d5">"regulation, security"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-124263e81aa4861b3ff954415c389034</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE CYBERSPACE ADMINISTRATION&quot;" target="&quot;OVERSEAS ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL&quot;">
  <data key="d3">18.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The State cyberspace administration can restrict or prohibit the provision of personal information to overseas organizations or individuals who violate Chinese regulations."</data>
  <data key="d5">"regulation, restriction"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE CYBERSPACE ADMINISTRATION&quot;" target="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The state cyberspace administration coordinates the work of the departments performing duties of personal information protection."</data>
  <data key="d5">"coordination, supervision"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;STATE ORGAN&quot;" target="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments may order rectification and impose sanctions on state organs that fail to perform their personal information protection obligations."</data>
  <data key="d5">"oversight, sanction"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;FOREIGN JUDICIAL OR LAW ENFORCEMENT AGENCIES&quot;" target="&quot;COMPETENT AUTHORITY OF THE PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The competent authority approves or denies requests from foreign judicial or law enforcement agencies for access to personal information stored in China."</data>
  <data key="d5">"approval, access control"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-34e103dd49e0435199d7ba0070490fa3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;RELEVANT DEPARTMENTS UNDER THE STATE COUNCIL&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Relevant departments under the State Council are part of the departments performing duties of personal information protection."</data>
  <data key="d5">"organizational structure, responsibility"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;LOCAL PEOPLE'S GOVERNMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Local people's governments are included among the departments performing duties of personal information protection."</data>
  <data key="d5">"organizational structure, responsibility"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION LEAKAGE, FALSIFICATION, OR LOSS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"In case of data breaches, the processor must inform the relevant departments."</data>
  <data key="d5">"reporting, accountability"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-16ff96468cd6ce50b600332542403f54</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSORS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">18.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments oversee and regulate the activities of personal information processors, enforcing compliance with the law and issuing penalties for violations.  They investigate and take action against those who violate the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"regulation, enforcement, penalty"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC SECURITY ORGAN&quot;">
  <data key="d3">16.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments refer criminal cases related to illegal personal information processing to the public security organ for legal action."</data>
  <data key="d5">"case referral, criminal justice"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;PEOPLE'S PROCURATORATE&quot;">
  <data key="d3">14.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments may collaborate with or report to the People's procuratorate in cases of widespread personal information infringement affecting numerous individuals."</data>
  <data key="d5">"collaboration, legal action"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL REPRESENTATIVE OR PERSON CHIEFLY IN CHARGE OF THE PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSOR&quot;">
  <data key="d3">16.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments may interview the legal representative to investigate potential violations or security incidents."</data>
  <data key="d5">"investigation, compliance"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;COMPLAINANTS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Departments receive and process complaints from complainants regarding illegal personal information processing."</data>
  <data key="d5">"complaint handling, redress"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;REPORTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">8.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"Departments receive and process reports from reporters regarding illegal personal information processing."</data>
  <data key="d5">"report handling, redress"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;SMALL PERSONAL INFORMATION PROCESSORS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">7.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments create specific rules and standards for small personal information processors."</data>
  <data key="d5">"rulemaking, guidance"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;RELEVANT ORGANIZATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d3">6.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments support relevant organizations in carrying out assessment and certification services."</data>
  <data key="d5">"support, collaboration"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;STAFF OF DEPARTMENTS RESPONSIBLE FOR PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">9.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments are responsible for the actions of their staff and may impose sanctions for misconduct. "</data>
  <data key="d5">"accountability, sanction"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEPARTMENTS PERFORMING DUTIES OF PERSONAL INFORMATION PROTECTION&quot;" target="&quot;PERSONAL INFORMATION&quot;">
  <data key="d3">10.0</data>
  <data key="d4">"The departments are responsible for protecting Personal Information according to the law."</data>
  <data key="d5">"protection, enforcement"</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-737a538d85e2897e75f31df035b55774</data>
</edge>
